        "original_id": "567c04af-00e6-5fd7-9283-d3373c5ca38c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sila Region, Dar Sila, Chad, Ouaddaï Region, Libya, Sudan, Central African Republic, Cameroon, Nigeria, Niger, Markounda\n- Topics: administrative divisions, national borders\n\nFacts:\n- Sila, also called Dar Sila, is a region of Chad that was created in 2008.\n- Sila Region was formed from the departments of Sila and Djourf Al Ahmar, which had previously been part of Ouaddaï Region.\n- Chad is bordered by Libya to the north, Sudan to the east, the Central African Republic to the south, Cameroon and Nigeria to the southwest, and Niger to the west.\n- Markounda is a sub-prefecture that borders Chad.",
